{"id":"api-example-001","type":"api_behavior","fact":"Example: Prisma findMany returns an empty array [] when no records match, not null.","recommendation":"Check .length instead of checking for null/undefined.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"Prisma docs","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["prisma","database","queries"],"affectedFiles":["src/lib/services/**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"api-bruno-collection-prerequest","type":"api_behavior","fact":"Bruno CLI (@usebruno/cli) supports script:pre-request in collection.bru under recursive (-r) runs — the hook fires before every request. Node built-ins plus 'axios' are available in the sandbox via require().","recommendation":"Use collection.bru's script:pre-request for idempotent auth bootstrap (check if accessToken is empty → POST /api/auth/login → bru.setVar). Guard with a _authBootstrapFailed flag to prevent rate-limit amplification on repeated login failures. Fallback if this ever breaks: a seq-0 _auth-bootstrap/login.bru folder.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"agent","reference":"Issue #28 WU-002 spike","date":"2026-04-13"}],"tags":["bruno","collection","pre-request","auth","axios"],"affectedFiles":["bruno/collection.bru"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"api-post-posts-response","type":"api_behavior","fact":"`POST /api/posts` returns `{post: {id, ...}, revision: {id, ...}}` — NOT `{id}` directly. The post creation flow includes the auto-created initial revision in the response.","recommendation":"Destructure as `const { post: { id: createdPostId } } = await res.json();`. Plan templates that wrote `const { id } = await res.json()` are wrong.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU3","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["api","posts","response-shape"],"affectedFiles":["e2e/specs/**/*.spec.ts","packages/server/src/routes/posts.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"api-vote-bookmark-singular","type":"api_behavior","fact":"Vote and bookmark mutation routes are SINGULAR: `POST /api/posts/:id/vote` (votes.ts:9) and `POST /api/posts/:id/bookmark` (bookmarks.ts:15). There is no `GET /api/posts/:id/votes` or per-post `/bookmarks` GET. `GET /api/bookmarks` (no `:id`) lists the user's own bookmarks.","recommendation":"Use singular paths for vote/bookmark mutations. For verification (e.g., cascade-delete), don't probe per-resource GETs that don't exist; assert `GET /api/posts/:id` returns 404 instead.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU4 cascade","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["api","votes","bookmarks","routes"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/votes.ts","packages/server/src/routes/bookmarks.ts","e2e/specs/**/*.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"api-update-post-no-isdraft","type":"api_behavior","fact":"`updatePostSchema` (packages/shared/src/validators/post.ts:46-53) does NOT accept `isDraft`. `PATCH /api/posts/:id { isDraft: false }` returns 400 zod-validation-error.","recommendation":"Use the dedicated `POST /api/posts/:id/publish` endpoint (posts.ts:217) to flip is_draft to false. The publish endpoint takes no body and is owner-gated.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #47 WU5 publish","date":"2026-04-29"}],"tags":["api","posts","publish","schema"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/posts.ts","packages/shared/src/validators/post.ts","e2e/specs/posts/publish-*.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-29T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id":"api-post-posts-response-envelope","type":"api_behavior","fact":"`POST /api/posts` returns `{ post: toPost(postRow), revision: toRevision(revisionRow) }` — TWO separate top-level fields, NOT a single PostWithRevision object. The revision id is at `response.revision.id`, NOT `response.post.revisionId`. Verified at packages/server/src/routes/posts.ts:106-110.","recommendation":"Destructure as: `const { post: { id: postId }, revision: { id: revisionId } } = await response.json()`. This differs from GET /api/posts/:id which returns `{ post: PostWithRevision }` (envelope-wrapped, revision nested inside post — see `gotcha-get-posts-id-response-envelope`).","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"session","reference":"Issue #48 Spec 1.8 inline-on-revision-line — REV 1 destructured incorrectly, fixed in REV 2","date":"2026-04-30"}],"tags":["api","posts","response-envelope","revision-id"],"affectedFiles":["packages/server/src/routes/posts.ts","e2e/specs/**/*.spec.ts"],"affectedServices":["api"],"createdAt":"2026-04-30T18:09:39Z","updatedAt":"2026-04-30T18:09:39Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
